## Who I Am

I'm Ronnie Alfaro, an engineering leader and AI systems builder with more than two decades of experience across infrastructure, operations, software engineering, DevOps, incident management, cloud platforms, and technical leadership.

Today I focus on designing and building AI systems that transform information into actionable knowledge. My interests span retrieval-augmented generation, semantic search, autonomous agents, knowledge systems, developer tooling, and automation at scale.

## What I Do

My work sits at the intersection of:

* Artificial Intelligence
* Semantic Search
* Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)
* Autonomous Agents
* Developer Tooling
* Automation
* Engineering Leadership
* Knowledge Systems

I am particularly interested in systems that reduce complexity, accelerate decision-making, and help people navigate large volumes of information.

## Selected Projects

### Semra

A knowledge-discovery system built around a simple question:

*How do we find what our documentation doesn't know?*

Semra reverses the traditional RAG model by identifying information that falls outside the existing knowledge base instead of retrieving what is already documented. Using semantic distance analysis, statistical novelty detection, and agent-driven workflows, it automatically discovers documentation gaps, generates draft articles, and creates GitLab merge requests for human review.

### RagIT

An AI-powered literary analysis platform that transforms books into searchable knowledge systems using embeddings, vector search, retrieval pipelines, and narrative-aware exploration.

### Arxiv Sanity Lite Modern

A modern resurrection of the classic research discovery platform, designed to help researchers and engineers navigate large collections of scientific literature.

### Obsidian Remote Notes

A lightweight synchronization platform that extends personal knowledge management workflows beyond a single device.

### Rustdrel

A terminal-based roguelike card game written in Rust, combining procedural gameplay, modular architecture, and classic command-line aesthetics.

## Leadership

Beyond building software, I lead engineering teams.

Throughout my career I have worked on scaling organizations, improving operational excellence, developing engineers, and helping teams navigate complex technical challenges.

I believe great engineering emerges from strong systems, clear communication, operational discipline, and continuous learning.

